Package: Bora
Title: Tissue Segmentation from Calibrated H&E Images
Version: 0.2.3
Authors@R: person("Stefano", "Cacciatore", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "stefano.cacciatore@icgeb.org")
Description: An R interface to the Bora tissue segmentation pipeline. The
    package prepares Virchow2 feature caches, fits class-aware predictors,
    and creates supervised or KODAMA-guided tissue masks. Python model inference
    is accessed through reticulate and CPU tile operations use compiled code.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.3.0)
Imports: jsonlite, Rcpp, reticulate
LinkingTo: Rcpp
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), knitr, rmarkdown, KODAMA, RANN, igraph, gpuinfo,
    SeuratObject, Giotto, SpatialExperiment, SummarizedExperiment
Config/testthat/edition: 3
VignetteBuilder: knitr
SystemRequirements: C++17; Python with the Bora encoder dependencies for
    Virchow2 inference; CUDA-enabled PyTorch for backend='cuda';
    huggingface_hub for optional model download
URL: https://github.com/tkcaccia/Bora
BugReports: https://github.com/tkcaccia/Bora/issues
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
